     "<div dir=\"ltr\">sorry, it&#39;s my first time use the shiny. would you tell me more detailedly. when I publish it, the web will popuplike this:<div><u></u><u></u><br></div><div>and my r code about sql is follow:</div><div>```{r}</div><div>  jHome &lt;- &#39;/System/Library/Frameworks/JavaVM.framework&#39;</div><div>  Sys.setenv(JAVA_HOME=jHome)</div><div>  options(java.parameters=&quot;-Xmx2g&quot;)</div><div>  library(rJava)</div><div>  .jinit()</div><div>  print(.jcall(&quot;java/lang/System&quot;, &quot;S&quot;, &quot;getProperty&quot;,&quot;java.version&quot;))</div><div>  library(RJDBC)</div><div>  jdbcDriver &lt;- JDBC(driverClass=&quot;oracle.jdbc.OracleDriver&quot;,classPath=&quot;~/ojdbc6.jar&quot;)</div><div>  dbHost  &lt;- &quot;115.***.***.***&quot;</div><div>  dbPort  &lt;- &quot;1521&quot;</div><div>  srvName &lt;- &quot;orcl&quot;</div><div>  dbUser  &lt;- &quot;***&quot;</div><div>  dbPass  &lt;- &quot;******&quot;</div><div>  conStr &lt;- paste(&quot;jdbc:oracle:thin:@//&quot;, dbHost, &quot;:&quot;, dbPort, &quot;/&quot;, srvName, sep = &quot;&quot;)</div><div>  jdbcConnection &lt;- dbConnect(jdbcDriver, conStr, dbUser, dbPass)</div><div>  data&lt;- dbGetQuery(jdbcConnection, &quot;select * from table&quot;)</div><div>  dbDisconnect(jdbcConnection)```<br></div></div>"
